{"ord":1,"off":0,"sha":"8379a9d692a9","bytes":4559,"id":"01a0ce82-83ea-7360-b77a-2900c5a4119e:request","call":"01a0ce82-83ea-7360-b77a-2900c5a4119e","run":"01a0ce82-66d4-7553-bc46-342573d999e8","model":"deepseek.v3.2","parts":[{"k":"data","data":"Here is a summary of the conversation to date:\n\n## SESSION INTENT\nDiagnose performance issues within the microservices system to identify the root cause of latency degradation.\n\n## SUMMARY\nThe checkout service has severe performance degradation (p99 latency: 2350ms vs. 410ms an hour ago, 1.2% error rate). Analysis identified calls to the payment service as a major contributor (p99: 2210ms). The payment service is confirmed as the primary root cause, showing the most severe degradation (p99 latency: 2190ms vs. 220ms an hour ago, 1.9% error rate). A critical finding is that the payment service's database connection pool is completely saturated (20/20 connections in use), causing high wait times (p99: 1840ms) for database connections. The inventory service was checked and is performing normally (p99: 61ms, stable, 0% error rate) and is not contributing to the issues. The user has asked which of the three services (checkout, payment, inventory) is in the worst state.\n\n## ARTIFACTS\nNone\n\n## NEXT STEPS\nAnswer the user's question by comparing the states of the checkout, payment, and inventory services to determine which is in the worst state.","state":"available","bytes":1167},{"k":"data","data":{"schema":"provider_body/1","role":"request","src":"runs-20260923T134415.145428000Z-000002.request","sha256":"8379a9d692a98a9afe865de8bb570adcce9c89203618f2954f723bf511508412","bytes":4559,"depth":0,"chain":"bd8ee0f881edc62a","model":"deepseek.v3.2","session":"ls-history-history-middleware-7bf102b808e4","run":"01a0ce82-66d4-7553-bc46-342573d999e8","call":"01a0ce82-83ea-7360-b77a-2900c5a4119e","segments":[{"lit":"{\"messages\":[[{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain\",\"schema\",\"messages\",\"SystemMessage\"],\